<title>UK: Novorossiisk, Ventspils oil ports reopen.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk, Ventspils oil ports reopen.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russia port of Novorossiisk and Latvia's Ventspils were open on Tuesday, after having being shut for most of the past week due to bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk, Russia's main oil export terminal, reopened late on Monday, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>Three crude tankers were alongside and waiting to load and another eight crude tankers were at anchor waiting to dock.</p>
<p>Ventspils, which closed at 0200 local time on Sunday reopened on Tuesday morning.</p>
<p>The crude pipeline running to the terminal at the Russian Black Sea port of Tuapse was reported to be closed. There were no details on when it would reopen.</p>
<p>The Ukrainian Black Sea oil port of Odessa was operating normally.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714.</p>
